    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d693">

                <pb facs="0719" n="621" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg621"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.113/1244: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-05-21T14:00:00+08:00">May 21, 1930—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 21—9:05 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>353. Department’s 165, May 13, 6 p.m. Following telegram has been received from
                    the Minister: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“May 19, 5 p.m. I have informed the Foreign Office that regulations
                            cannot be regarded as applicable pending receipt of instructions from
                            the Department.”<anchor n="87" xml:id="d693-f1"/></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d693-f1" n="87" xml:id="d693-f1-content">
                <p>The Chinese Ministry for Foreign Affairs in a note dated May 23, 1930, informed
                    the Minister in China of the promulgation of revised regulations, a copy of
                    which was enclosed (893.113/1256).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
